Package: consensusRegions
Type: Package
Title: Consensus Regions from Replicated ChIP-seq and ATAC-seq Experiments
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: person("Sebastian", "Gregoricchio",
                  email = "s.gregoricchio@nki.nl",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9209-5403"))
Description: Merges the evidence carried by replicated ChIP-seq, ATAC-seq
    or CUT&RUN experiments into a single set of consensus regions. When
    several replicates agree on a position their p-values are combined, so
    that a peak too weak to survive on its own can still be retained.
    Fisher, Stouffer, Lancaster and rank-product combinations are
    available; the weighted ones accept per-replicate weights taken from
    FRiP scores, library sizes, or the peak sets themselves when no
    alignment file is at hand. Input can be anything from a full
    narrowPeak to a bare BED3: scores are rank-transformed when p-values
    are missing, and a weighted k-of-n presence rule takes over when even
    the score is absent. The threshold on the combined significance can be
    calibrated against a permutation null rather than fixed a priori.
    Quality control plots and export to SummarizedExperiment are included.
